With regards to your message at 10:09 PM 4/3/04, Mike Tibor. Where you stated:
>On Sat, 3 Apr 2004, Jeff DeMaagd wrote:
>
> > Ricardo Ramos wrote:
> > > Use PC100, not PC133
> >
> > Isn't PC133 backward compatible with PC100?
>
>Yes, PC133 will work fine.
>
>Mike


Not always.
The motherboard checks the RAM speed with SPD pin data on the module, and 
if it can not recognize the code, it will consider it invalid. SOME PC133 
may work, other types may not.
If I recall the LX also wants to see 16 x 8 RAM chip layout ( in a 128MB 
module), not more density using less numbers of chips.




